<section image-layout="blank" id="eegalualJs" background-color="heading"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="QPZ7Pvyh9N" vertical-align="center" colspan="35"><p role="eyebrow">Visual communication · Media evolution</p><h1 font-size="44pt">The page changed its behavior</h1><p font-size="lg">The page did not disappear. It changed from fixed arrangement, to interactive surface, to variable output.</p><spacer size="24pt"></spacer><hr color="accent" thickness="md" width="xs"><p><b>Thesis:</b> media evolution reorganizes production, distribution, interaction, and authorship. It does not guarantee improvement.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="sdVUHjGz-L" padding="0" colspan="25"><grid direction="vertical" spacing="none"><grid-item id="756UDBpbrf" padding="0" rowspan="52"><img src="https://cdn-staging.gamma.app/QWjS6fBfpt/generated-images/u0NlYkazBUh_CQgo9NLgg.png" saved-media-id="gq70rd11z5uaxu9" source="image.ai-generated" background="true" image-style="editorial-media-study" alt="Large-format editorial studio photograph of one page-like media mechanism evolving across three aligned stages: a rigid archive-buff paper frame, a linked screen-grey window, and several variable sheets emerging along vermilion plotter paths, arranged as a precise material study under cool raking daylight on warm paper, carbon black structural elements, generous negative space, no text or lettering" meta="{&quot;width&quot;:1248,&quot;height&quot;:1664}"></grid-item><grid-item id="2GtyIQ1AfO" background-color="surface" padding="10pt 14pt" rowspan="8"><p role="caption">Conceptual media study · not archival evidence</p></grid-item></grid></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="reIb1gQvt_" vertical-align="center"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="8tfcHvCDtG"><p role="eyebrow">Analytical lens · System before surface</p><h2>A medium is a system</h2><grid spacing="medium" vertical-sizing="fill"><grid-item id="0OTmEEpSfq" vertical-align="center" colspan="25"><p>Tools and formats shape what can be made. Infrastructures shape circulation. Interfaces shape perception, while conventions shape participation.</p><grid divider="sm neutral-border" direction="vertical" vertical-sizing="hug"><grid-item id="MiBUoAaP_3" padding="9pt 0"><p><b>Fixed instance</b> · Print stabilizes a version.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="NDwS-PiYhV" padding="9pt 0"><p><b>Coded state</b> · Digital systems update and respond.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="aZncbvht3z" padding="9pt 0"><p><b>Generated variation</b> · Computational systems generate and vary.</p></grid-item></grid><p font-size="sm">Transformation occurs when these relationships change—not when a surface merely looks new.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="BDqsP84Hhe" align="center" vertical-align="center" colspan="35"><diagram template-key="inputs" align="center" width="500pt" height="320pt" data-meta="{&quot;general&quot;:[{&quot;text&quot;:&quot;<h4>Medium as a system</h4>&quot;}],&quot;step&quot;:[{&quot;text&quot;:&quot;<h4>Tools &amp; formats</h4><p>Define what can be created</p>&quot;},{&quot;text&quot;:&quot;<h4>Infrastructure</h4><p>Determines how work circulates</p>&quot;},{&quot;text&quot;:&quot;<h4>Interfaces</h4><p>Shape perception and access</p>&quot;},{&quot;text&quot;:&quot;<h4>Conventions</h4><p>Organize participation</p>&quot;}]}"></diagram></grid-item></grid></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="CsxWpZLAQW" vertical-align="center"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="zpIpZh1Bcq"><p role="eyebrow">Era 01 · Fixed instance</p><h2>Print stabilizes space</h2><grid spacing="medium"><grid-item id="-N86ISHZHB" colspan="35"><custom-code>
            <style>
              .forme-study { width: 100%; font-family: var(--body-font); color: var(--body-color); }
              .forme-study svg { display: block; width: 100%; height: 17em; }
              .forme-study .chase { fill: color-mix(in srgb, var(--palette-2) 48%, var(--card-color)); stroke: var(--body-color); stroke-width: 3; }
              .forme-study .unit { fill: var(--card-color); stroke: var(--body-color); stroke-width: 1.5; }
              .forme-study .active { fill: var(--accent-color); stroke: var(--accent-color); }
              .forme-study .rule { stroke: var(--body-color); stroke-width: 2; fill: none; }
              .forme-study .accent-rule { stroke: var(--accent-color); stroke-width: 3; fill: none; }
              .forme-study text { font-family: var(--body-font); fill: var(--body-color); font-size: 0.72em; }
              .forme-study .small { font-size: 0.6em; letter-spacing: 0.05em; }
              .forme-study .mirror { font-family: var(--heading-font); font-size: 1.2em; font-weight: 700; }
            </style>
            <div class="forme-study">
              <svg viewBox="0 0 560 270" width="560" height="270" role="img" aria-label="Schematic movable-type forme showing separate mirrored units locked into a frame before inking">
                <text x="42" y="20" class="small">SEPARATE, MIRRORED UNITS</text>
                <rect x="40" y="35" width="350" height="190" rx="2" class="chase"></rect>
                <rect x="62" y="58" width="44" height="42" class="unit"></rect>
                <rect x="112" y="58" width="44" height="42" class="unit"></rect>
                <rect x="162" y="58" width="44" height="42" class="active"></rect>
                <rect x="212" y="58" width="44" height="42" class="unit"></rect>
                <rect x="262" y="58" width="44" height="42" class="unit"></rect>
                <rect x="312" y="58" width="44" height="42" class="unit"></rect>
                <rect x="62" y="107" width="44" height="42" class="unit"></rect>
                <rect x="112" y="107" width="44" height="42" class="unit"></rect>
                <rect x="162" y="107" width="44" height="42" class="unit"></rect>
                <rect x="212" y="107" width="44" height="42" class="unit"></rect>
                <rect x="262" y="107" width="44" height="42" class="active"></rect>
                <rect x="312" y="107" width="44" height="42" class="unit"></rect>
                <rect x="62" y="156" width="44" height="42" class="unit"></rect>
                <rect x="112" y="156" width="44" height="42" class="unit"></rect>
                <rect x="162" y="156" width="44" height="42" class="unit"></rect>
                <rect x="212" y="156" width="44" height="42" class="unit"></rect>
                <rect x="262" y="156" width="44" height="42" class="unit"></rect>
                <rect x="312" y="156" width="44" height="42" class="unit"></rect>
                <g transform="translate(95 88) scale(-1 1)"><text class="mirror">A</text></g>
                <g transform="translate(245 88) scale(-1 1)"><text class="mirror">R</text></g>
                <g transform="translate(145 137) scale(-1 1)"><text class="mirror">G</text></g>
                <g transform="translate(345 186) scale(-1 1)"><text class="mirror">D</text></g>
                <path d="M390 130 H470" class="accent-rule"></path>
                <path d="M458 120 L475 130 L458 140" class="accent-rule"></path>
                <text x="422" y="108" class="small">INK</text>
                <rect x="478" y="72" width="58" height="118" class="unit"></rect>
                <line x1="490" y1="92" x2="524" y2="92" class="rule"></line>
                <line x1="490" y1="110" x2="524" y2="110" class="rule"></line>
                <line x1="490" y1="128" x2="516" y2="128" class="rule"></line>
                <line x1="490" y1="154" x2="524" y2="154" class="rule"></line>
                <text x="477" y="215" class="small">REPEATABLE COPY</text>
                <text x="42" y="250" class="small">THE CHASE LOCKS SPATIAL DECISIONS BEFORE DISTRIBUTION</text>
              </svg>
            </div>
          </custom-code><p role="caption">Schematic reading of a movable-type forme · not an archival reproduction</p></grid-item><grid-item id="ZfTfQ-id_3" vertical-align="center" colspan="25"><labels><label variant="solid">Material logic</label></labels><h3>Composition becomes repeatable</h3><p>Type, margins, sequence, and edition stabilize hierarchy across copies. Revision occurs before distribution; readers mainly encounter a finished arrangement.</p><p>The forme makes this logic visible: letters remain separate, mirrored units until they are locked into a physical grid before ink reaches paper.</p></grid-item></grid></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="9T2H_ELm4t" vertical-align="center"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="RC7Ip2R_6E"><p role="eyebrow">Era 02 · Coded state</p><h2>The document joins a network</h2><p>A page becomes a maintained, networked version rather than a distributed finished copy.</p><smart-layout variant="minimalTimeline" orientation="horizontal" two-sided="true" cell-size="15"><smart-layout-item><h4>1989 · The proposal</h4><p>Tim Berners-Lee proposes the Web at CERN.</p></smart-layout-item><smart-layout-item><h4>30 April 1993 · Public domain</h4><p>CERN makes Web software freely available.</p></smart-layout-item><smart-layout-item><h4>The networked page</h4><p>Addressable, linkable, updateable, and connected to user action.</p></smart-layout-item></smart-layout><grid spacing="small" vertical-sizing="hug"><grid-item id="TelKdFQdqr" cell-style="subtle" colspan="15"><h4>Addressable</h4></grid-item><grid-item id="E2BHRJFM-u" cell-style="subtle" colspan="15"><h4>Linkable</h4></grid-item><grid-item id="h_WFKlDWa3" cell-style="subtle" colspan="15"><h4>Updateable</h4></grid-item><grid-item id="1Twn9b4Ea_" cell-style="subtle" colspan="15"><h4>Responsive</h4></grid-item></grid><p role="caption">Source: <a href="https://home.cern/science/computing/the-birth-of-the-web/">CERN, “The birth of the Web”</a></p></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="57sLOYhS9H"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="5nLmNAYbYI"><p role="eyebrow">Three-era comparison · Dominant tendencies</p><h2>What changes across the three eras?</h2><table col-widths="[16,28,28,28]" header-row="true" header-col="true" borders="all" striped="false"><tbody><tr><td><p>Dimension</p></td><td background-color="palette-2"><p>Print · Fixed instance</p></td><td background-color="palette-3"><p>Digital · Coded state</p></td><td background-color="accent"><p>Computational · Generated variation</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>Production</p></td><td valign="middle"><p>Composed instance</p></td><td valign="middle"><p>Coded state</p></td><td valign="middle"><p>Generated variation</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>Distribution</p></td><td valign="middle"><p>Editions and physical circulation</p></td><td valign="middle"><p>Network access and maintained versions</p></td><td valign="middle"><p>On-demand synthesis</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>Audience</p></td><td valign="middle"><p>Reader</p></td><td valign="middle"><p>User</p></td><td valign="middle"><p>Participant and evaluator</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>Authorship</p></td><td valign="middle"><p>Visible makers</p></td><td valign="middle"><p>Collaborative technical stacks</p></td><td valign="middle"><p>People, data, models, and interfaces</p></td></tr></tbody></table><aside><p>These are overlapping analytical lenses, not sealed eras. Each newer system carries older forms—and their assumptions—inside it.</p></aside></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="BEYU4ODIlj" vertical-align="center"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="ia5gtTPcKs"><p role="eyebrow">Era 03 · Generated variation</p><h2>Computational intelligence makes the output variable</h2><p>The designer increasingly specifies a space of possible outputs rather than one resolved artifact.</p><smart-layout variant="cycle" cell-size="10"><smart-layout-item><h4>Intent + constraints</h4></smart-layout-item><smart-layout-item><h4>Data, rules, or prompt</h4></smart-layout-item><smart-layout-item><h4>Model computation</h4></smart-layout-item><smart-layout-item><h4>Output</h4></smart-layout-item><smart-layout-item><h4>Human judgment</h4></smart-layout-item><smart-layout-item><h4>Revision</h4></smart-layout-item></smart-layout><grid spacing="medium" vertical-sizing="hug"><grid-item id="dCQjsPlGmU" cell-style="subtle" colspan="30"><h4>What scales</h4><p>Variation, adaptation, and repeated synthesis across contexts.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="n6WvFgZCVM" background-color="accent" colspan="30"><h4>What becomes design work</h4><p>Provenance, opacity, bias, evaluation, and the conditions for responsible revision.</p></grid-item></grid></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="q-E8Z8wKWW" vertical-align="center"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="AfrZPTs4bB"><p role="eyebrow">Accumulation, not replacement</p><h2>Progress is not a staircase</h2><grid spacing="medium"><grid-item id="LbFm63NsEF" background-color="palette-2" colspan="20"><h3>Print</h3><p>Stable, inspectable composition. Revision is slower, and circulation remains materially constrained.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="FvXknDeBTR" background-color="palette-3" colspan="20"><h3>Digital</h3><p>Access, interaction, and rapid updates. Dependence, volatility, and distraction enter the experience.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="lpfYeEKslh" background-color="accent" colspan="20"><h3>Computational</h3><p>Variation and scale. Opacity, homogenization, and uncertain provenance complicate judgment.</p></grid-item></grid><custom-code>
        <style>
          .era-overlap { width: 100%; font-family: var(--body-font); color: var(--body-color); padding-top: 0.5em; }
          .era-overlap .overlap-title { font-family: var(--heading-font); font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 0.55em; }
          .era-overlap .track { position: relative; height: 6.4em; border-left: 1px solid var(--body-color); border-right: 1px solid var(--body-color); }
          .era-overlap .bar { position: absolute; height: 1.45em; display: flex; align-items: center; padding-left: 0.75em; font-size: 0.78em; font-weight: 600; }
          .era-overlap .print { top: 0; left: 0; width: 100%; background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--palette-2) 72%, var(--card-color)); }
          .era-overlap .digital { top: 2.1em; left: 24%; width: 76%; background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--palette-3) 72%, var(--card-color)); }
          .era-overlap .computational { top: 4.2em; left: 52%; width: 48%; background: var(--accent-color); color: var(--card-color); }
        </style>
        <div class="era-overlap">
          <div class="overlap-title">Media persist inside one another</div>
          <div class="track" aria-label="Schematic overlap of print, digital, and computational media">
            <div class="bar print">Print systems continue</div>
            <div class="bar digital">Digital systems join them</div>
            <div class="bar computational">Computational systems accumulate</div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </custom-code><p role="caption">Schematic overlap · not a chronological scale</p><p>Designers choose and combine systems according to purpose, audience, and consequence—not novelty alone.</p></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="RuwL2MW5Yj" background-color="heading"><grid spacing="medium"><grid-item id="m2L_NYyRC5" colspan="25"><p role="eyebrow">Studio method · Five questions</p><h1 font-size="40pt">Design the conditions, not only the artifact</h1><p font-size="lg">Read the medium by tracing what it permits, distributes, conceals, and asks the audience to become.</p><spacer mode="fill"></spacer><grid spacing="none" vertical-sizing="hug"><grid-item id="njMs_qaPYH" background-color="surface" padding="16pt 18pt"><p role="eyebrow">Studio prompt</p><p>Translate one message across print, interactive, and generative forms. Keep intent constant; document how roles change.</p></grid-item></grid></grid-item><grid-item id="V7pqXhck1T" vertical-align="center" colspan="35"><grid divider="sm palette-5" marker="number" marker-style="solid" marker-shape="circle" marker-position="inline" marker-numbering-format="decimal-leading-zero" direction="vertical" style="--marker-inline-size: 32pt; --marker-gap: 14pt;"><grid-item id="YmjjUfUnn7" padding="12pt 0"><h4>What is fixed, and what can vary?</h4></grid-item><grid-item id="U23H7TYI6S" padding="12pt 0"><h4>Who can make, publish, revise, and respond?</h4></grid-item><grid-item id="Crkrh5ADLA" padding="12pt 0"><h4>How does the work travel?</h4></grid-item><grid-item id="_KJ2PsOLlh" padding="12pt 0"><h4>Where are decisions visible or hidden?</h4></grid-item><grid-item id="4j2f_RVD3P" padding="12pt 0"><h4>What does the interface ask the audience to become?</h4></grid-item></grid></grid-item></grid></section>